      1: 'Practice can improve some tasks, but decision-fatigue claims concern possible deterioration or strategic shifts after repeated choice. A general calibration benefit does not capture the contested phenomenon.',
      3: 'Neurological fatigue in demyelinating disease has distinct clinical and biological considerations. Similar everyday language does not make the proposed judgment effect the same medical condition.',
